[KiCad-IOS port] kiplatform: add the wxQt port implementation

kiplatform selects its UI/WEBVIEW implementation by KICAD_WX_PORT
(osx/msw/gtk). For "qt" it selected nothing, so every KIPLATFORM::UI
symbol (IsDarkTheme, ForceFocus, GetContentScaleFactor, ...) was
undefined when linking libkicommon — the only link error class in the
desktop wxQt catalogue once compilation was clean.

This patch adds the missing port:
- libs/kiplatform/CMakeLists.txt: qt branch selecting the new files.
- libs/kiplatform/port/wxqt/ui.cpp (new): KIPLATFORM::UI implemented
  wx-generically on top of Qt-backed wxWidgets — system colours and
  scale factors from wxSystemSettings/wxWindow, focus via SetFocus +
  Raise. macOS/GTK-only workarounds (child-window ordering, cmd-key
  collisions, cell-layout hacks, Wayland confinement, overlay
  scrolling, IME fixups) are no-ops, mirroring how the existing ports
  no-op each other's platform hacks.
- libs/kiplatform/port/wxqt/webview.cpp (new): cookie functions report
  failure — wxQt has no wxWebView backend (wxUSE_WEBVIEW is OFF).

New files carry the standard KiCad GPL header. Modified/new files
(GPL-3.0-or-later, same license as upstream):
  libs/kiplatform/CMakeLists.txt (modified)
  libs/kiplatform/port/wxqt/ui.cpp (new)
  libs/kiplatform/port/wxqt/webview.cpp (new)

--- a/libs/kiplatform/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libs/kiplatform/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -11,6 +11,14 @@
         port/wxmsw/ui.cpp
         port/wxmsw/webview.cpp
         )
+elseif( KICAD_WX_PORT STREQUAL qt )
+    # [KiCad-IOS port] wxQt port implementation (wx-generic, via Qt):
+    # without this branch no KIPLATFORM::UI/WEBVIEW symbols are built
+    # for the qt port at all and every KiCad library fails to link.
+    set( PLATFORM_SRCS
+        port/wxqt/ui.cpp
+        port/wxqt/webview.cpp
+        )
 elseif( KICAD_WX_PORT STREQUAL gtk )
     set( PLATFORM_SRCS
         port/wxgtk/ui.cpp
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libs/kiplatform/port/wxqt/ui.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,239 @@
